<p>This policy describes {{ site.name }}, published by {{ site.legalName }}. It was last updated on October 27, 2026.</p>
<h2>Governing law</h2>
<p>This policy is issued by {{ site.legalName }}. It is governed by the laws of the State of Florida.</p>
<h2>What the site is</h2>
<p>The site is a set of static pages. It does not offer accounts or comments. The contact page can send a note through FormSubmit.co. This site does not keep its own copy of that note. It does not sell personal information. It shows third-party advertising served by Google, described below.</p>
<h2>Analytics</h2>
<p>Each HTML page loads a Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon from <code>https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js</code>. Cloudflare’s <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/web-analytics/about/">documentation</a> says the snippet collects page-view and visitor metrics with the browser Performance API, and that Web Analytics does not collect or use visitors’ personal data. That description is Cloudflare’s. Apart from Google Analytics (below) and Google’s advertising script, this site adds no other advertising or social-tracking script.</p>
<h2>Google Analytics 4</h2>
<p>With your consent, the site uses Google Analytics 4, a service of Google LLC, to understand how many people visit and which pages they read. Google Analytics collects information such as the pages you view, how you arrived (referrer), approximate location derived from your IP address, device, browser and screen type, and interactions such as scrolls and clicks. Google Analytics 4 does not log or store full IP addresses. The site does not send your name, email address or other directly identifying information to Google Analytics.</p>
<p>Google Analytics sets first-party cookies named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code>, which distinguish visitors and sessions and typically last up to two years.</p>
<p><strong>Consent.</strong> The Google Analytics script is not loaded until you choose Accept in the cookie banner. The site uses Google Consent Mode v2 with analytics and advertising storage set to denied by default. If you choose Reject, Google Analytics is not loaded, and any Analytics cookies from an earlier Accept are deleted. Your choice is saved in your browser’s local storage under <code>mtm-analytics-consent</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Opting out.</strong> You can change your choice at any time with the Cookie settings link in the footer. You can also delete the cookies in your browser, or install Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. How Google handles this data is described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> and at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>Google Analytics cookies are set only after you accept, as described above. This site does not set its own advertising cookie, but Google and its partners may set cookies when ads are served (see Advertising below). Your browser may also store ordinary technical data. Cloudflare’s beacon is described above. The host may use cookies or similar logs for its own service.</p>
<h2>Advertising</h2>
<p>This site uses Google AdSense. Google and its partners use cookies and similar technologies to serve and measure ads, which may be personalised. You can learn how Google uses data from sites that use its services at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">policies.google.com/technologies/ads</a>. Visitors in the EU, UK and Switzerland see a consent choice from Google before personalised advertising is used. Advertising never changes what this desk reports.</p>
<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may process technical logs, such as IP address, user agent, and the page requested, to operate and secure the host. That processing is described in the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
<h2>Messages you send</h2>
<p>The contact form sends your name, email address, and message to <a href="https://formsubmit.co/">FormSubmit.co</a>. FormSubmit.co is the processor for that delivery. It forwards the note to the publisher, {{ site.legalName }}. The message and email are used only to reply, to correct a story, or to fix the site. They are not sold or shared. A repository issue is handled the same way: it is used to reply or to fix the site. Do not send passwords, payment card numbers, or other secrets in a story tip.</p>
<h2>Links</h2>
<p>Stories link to other sites, including company blogs and help centers. Those sites have their own policies and are not covered by this one.</p>
<h2>Children</h2>
<p>The site is not directed at children under 13, and it does not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>When this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Privacy questions go to the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
